  "term": "seduction",
  "definition": "Seduction, in this psychology-ethics context, means a subtle form of influence that works mostly outside conscious awareness by shaping attention, preferences, and habits. It relies on personalized timing, design, and feedback to steer behavior rather than on direct reasoning or explicit persuasion.",
